The precise measurement of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate is crucial for determining the CKM matrix element $|V_{cs}|$ with high accuracy. To achieve this, we have conducted a comprehensive analysis of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate, considering various possible forms of the differential rate. By fitting these different forms to the data obtained from the Belle experiment, we have evaluated the impact of the differential rate's shape on the determination of $|V_{cs}|$. Our findings indicate that the precise shape of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate is not a significant factor in accurately determining the $|V_{cs}|$ matrix element.
